{"name":"Blind Date","hex":"#bcaea1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blind date","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A date (romantic meeting) between two people who have never met before."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blind_date"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blind date","blocks":[{"text":"A blind date is a romantic meeting between two people who have never met before."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blind_date"},{"title":"Blind Date (1934 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Blind Date is a 1934 American drama film directed by Roy William Neill and starring Ann Sothern, Neil Hamilton, and Paul Kelly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/97/Blind_Date_poster.jpg/330px-Blind_Date_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blind_Date_(1934_film)"},{"title":"Blind Date (British game show)","blocks":[{"text":"Blind Date is a British dating game show first produced by London Weekend Television (LWT). An unscreened pilot was made with comic Duncan Norvelle as presenter but it was eventually hosted by Cilla Black, who already hosted the LWT series Surprise Surprise. Blind Date originally ran on Saturday nights from 30 November 1985 to 31 May 2003 on ITV."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/96/Blind_Date_Titlecard_2018.png/330px-Blind_Date_Titlecard_2018.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blind_Date_(British_game_show)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/97/Blind_Date_poster.jpg/330px-Blind_Date_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/97/Blind_Date_poster.jpg/330px-Blind_Date_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/